---
title: "Shared derivations"
---

This file is the *one place* a derivation lives. Documents pull a single section
out of it with `{{< include _includes/shared-derivation.tmd#sec-id >}}`, so a post
series can share one statement of an argument without copy-paste drift.

Rendered on its own it is an ordinary document; nothing about a file makes it
"an include".

## The normal equations {#sec-normal-equations}

Minimizing $\lVert y - X\beta \rVert^2$ sets the gradient to zero:

$$
X^\top X \hat\beta = X^\top y
$$

so $\hat\beta = (X^\top X)^{-1} X^\top y$ whenever $X^\top X$ is invertible.

### Why the inverse can be avoided {#sec-normal-equations-qr}

In practice you factor rather than invert: a QR decomposition of $X$ solves the
same system with a far better condition number. This subsection is *inside*
`sec-normal-equations`, so transcluding that section brings this one with it.

## The bias-variance decomposition {#sec-bias-variance}

For squared-error loss the expected test error splits into three terms that add:

$$
\mathbb{E}\left[(y - \hat f(x))^2\right]
  = \operatorname{Bias}\left[\hat f(x)\right]^2
  + \operatorname{Var}\left[\hat f(x)\right]
  + \sigma^2
$$

The last term is irreducible, which is why no amount of model capacity drives the
error to zero.

## A section nobody transcludes {#sec-unused}

Kept deliberately: it is the control. A transclusion that pulled the whole file
would drag this paragraph in too, and the pin would not be able to tell the
difference.
